<article class="env-lemma" id="0D5S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D5S">Lemma <span data-tag="0D5S">20.27.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Y \to Z$ be morphisms of ringed spaces. Then $Lf^* \circ Lg^* = L(g \circ f)^*$ as functors $D(\mathcal{O}_ Z) \to D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $E$ be an object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ Z)$. By construction $Lg^*E$ is computed by choosing a K-flat complex $\mathcal{K}^\bullet $ representing $E$ on $Z$ and setting $Lg^*E = g^*\mathcal{K}^\bullet $. By Lemma <a href="/tag/06YC" data-tag="06YC">20.26.8</a> we see that $g^*\mathcal{K}^\bullet $ is K-flat on $Y$. Then $Lf^*Lg^*E$ is given by $f^*g^*\mathcal{K}^\bullet = (g \circ f)^*\mathcal{K}^\bullet $ which also represents $L(g \circ f)^*E$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>